  "explanation": "The question asks where the Boston and Maine Railroad Depot is located. Two documents (D1S1 and D2S1) directly name the 'Raymond Railroad Depot' as a historic former Boston and Maine railroad station located at 1 Depot Street in Raymond, New Hampshire (D1S1) and Salem, Massachusetts (D2S1). These are distinct locations for what appears to be the same named structure, likely due to a documentation error or confusion in naming. Since both are explicitly stated as the location of the Boston and Maine Railroad Depot, they are retained as separate valid answers. The third candidate (36 Pine Street in Stoneham, Massachusetts) refers to the Stoneham Railroad Depot, which is explicitly described as a different structure built by the Boston and Maine Railroad but not claimed to be the Boston and Maine Railroad Depot itself. Therefore, it is excluded."
